The bundle contains two valid RFC 3161 timestamps over the same signature. The
first timestamp is within the signing certificate's validity period, but the
second was issued after it expired. Verification must validate every supplied
timestamp rather than selecting only the earliest one.

Creation: copy the bundle and trusted root from `rekor2-happy-path`, then append
the RFC 3161 timestamp from `rekor2-timestamp-with-incorrect-time_fail`. Both
source bundles contain the same message signature. Remove line wrapping from
the appended timestamp's base64 encoding.
